\DOC ENSURES_EXISTING_PRESERVED_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_EXISTING_PRESERVED_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Given a state component, transforms an {ensures} goal so that its postcondition
additionally asserts that the component still holds the value given to it in
the precondition, and its frame is widened by a {MAYCHANGE} for that component.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {ctm : term} is the state component (as read by {read}) whose
value is to be carried from the precondition into the postcondition and added
to the frame relation. The goal's precondition must fix {read ctm} to some term
{t}. The resulting conclusion has the precondition and postcondition
conjunctions re-associated/flattened — parenthesised groups of conjuncts are
merged into a single right-nested conjunction, so the conjuncts themselves are
unchanged apart from bracketing, giving {P'} and {Q'} from {P} and {Q} — the
equation {read ctm s = t} taken from the precondition appended as a new final
conjunct of the postcondition, and {MAYCHANGE [ctm]} composed with {,,} onto
the end of the frame relation.
{
      A ?- ensures m P Q R
   =============================================================  ENSURES_EXISTING_PRESERVED_TAC ctm
      A ?- ensures m P' (Q' /\ read ctm s = t) (R ,, MAYCHANGE [ctm])
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of transformation, always on
{ensures} goals for the x86 model.

\ENDDOC
